{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"initial-full-source-ordered-load-readiness-review","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Initial full-source ordered load readiness review"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evidence by revision, on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fix-full-source-sync-readiness"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"First campaign: oracle commit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bc2c9438b"},{"type":"text","value":", production fix "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a73a35bac"},{"type":"text","value":". The\nRED results on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" and the first mutant results refer to this campaign."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After merging "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" with #2055 (merge "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"5d4802052"},{"type":"text","value":"): the eager and\njoined-filter witnesses and the merged-code mutant results in \"After merging\n#2055\" were run on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afef46744"},{"type":"text","value":", which adds those witnesses to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"5d4802052"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After merging "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" with #2060 (merge "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a0537aa0e"},{"type":"text","value":"): the ordered-lifecycle\nand loader oracles (332 tests) and every CI test group passed on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a0537aa0e"},{"type":"text","value":". The production gate is unchanged from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afef46744"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"contract-and-evidence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contract and evidence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"#1896 made an ordered, limited live query ready in the call that creates it\nwhen every acquisition for its initial window returns literal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" after\nits establishing receipts apply. Its stated exceptions are explicit window\nmoves, repair, truncate replay, and framework render timing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A plan that requires the full source (an inner or right join, a functional or\nresidual predicate, grouping, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"having"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"distinct"},{"type":"text","value":", an indirect order, or a\ncustom string comparator) loads its ordered source with one filtered\nfull-source request from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OrderedSourceLoader.start()"},{"type":"text","value":". The loader classified\nevery "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"full-source"},{"type":"text","value":" request as an authoritative repair, so this initial load\nwas excluded from the synchronous cut. On "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":", such a query over an eager\nsource, or over an on-demand source whose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loadSubset"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", reported\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loading"},{"type":"text","value":" with no rows at creation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The authority for the law is the #1896 cut in\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/src/query/live/ARCHITECTURE.md"},{"type":"text","value":" (initial readiness section) and\nthe #1896 pull request description, which states the rule for every ordered\nand limited query whose required source work finishes synchronously. This\nchange revises that section to name the initial full-source load and a later\nfull-source fallback explicitly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The fix classifies by purpose. The first full-source request of a loader that\nhas not settled a source request and owes no ordering repair is an initial\nload and may settle synchronously. A later full-source request keeps the\nasynchronous path."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"observations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observations"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fix"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On-demand, synchronous, 4 features (inner join, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fn.where"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"distinct"},{"type":"text","value":", custom collation)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{\"rows\":[],\"status\":\"loading\"}"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{\"rows\":[1,2],\"status\":\"ready\"}"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On-demand, Promise, 4 features"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"loading"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"loading"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Eager source, 4 features"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{\"rows\":[],\"status\":\"loading\"}"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{\"rows\":[1,2],\"status\":\"ready\"}"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Truncate replay, 4 features"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"prior window at the replay call, replacement a task later"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"same"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Warm readiness: full-source fallback after a settled ordered request (existing case)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"loading"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"loading"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React first layout commit, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fn.where"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"orderBy"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"limit"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"see review head"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ ids: ['1','2'], status: 'ready' }"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"mutant-results","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant results"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each mutant ran against "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tests/query/ordered-lifecycle-oracle.property.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcome"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gate keyed on request kind: every "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"full-source"},{"type":"text","value":" request settles synchronously"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assertion failure: warm readiness case, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expected 'ready' to be 'loading'"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Promise results may settle synchronously"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assertion failures in 145 tests"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Initial full-source load still excluded (the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" behavior)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assertion failures in the 4 synchronous on-demand cells"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Initial-load test without the settled-request condition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assertion failure: warm readiness case"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The truncate replay cells do not distinguish the kind-based mutant: replay\npublishes through the subscription's replay barrier, not this loader gate. The\nwarm readiness case is the distinguishing neighbour for that design."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"after-merging-2055","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After merging #2055"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Main check."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Before the merge, this branch's witnesses ran on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" at\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"25201da6c"},{"type":"text","value":" (which includes #2027 and #2055). All 8 synchronous full-source\ncells and the React first-commit witness still failed, for example\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Expected {\"rows\":[1,2],\"status\":\"ready\"}, received {\"rows\":[],\"status\":\"loading\"}"},{"type":"text","value":"\nand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expected { ids: [], status: 'loading' } to deeply equal { ids: [ '1', '2' ], status: 'ready' }"},{"type":"text","value":". #2027 changed the infinite-query hooks' "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startSync"},{"type":"text","value":", not this\ngate, so the gap remained."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combined gate."}]},{"type":"text","value":" An initial load of any kind, and an eager bounded\nordered-prefix repair (#2055), settle synchronously on literal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"(!isAuthoritativeRepair ||\n  isInitialFullSource ||\n  (this.readsBoundedPrefix && !isFullSource))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed expectation."}]},{"type":"text","value":" #2055 added "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keeps an eager full-source ordered window loading until its load settles"},{"type":"text","value":", pinning "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":"'s asynchronous timing while its\nown scope stayed narrow. Recorded predictions before the edit: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" and #2055\npredict "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{loading, 0 rows}"},{"type":"text","value":" at creation; this branch's law predicts\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ready, [4, 3]}"},{"type":"text","value":". The authority is #1896's rule and the user's decision to close\nthis gap. The test is now "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"publishes an eager full-source ordered window at creation"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Joined-filter interaction."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keeps the first eligible joined rows after a synchronous full-source load"},{"type":"text","value":" combines a function filter with #2055's\nLEFT-joined filter history: a label-only update to distant row 10, then a delete\nof visible row 2. The window moves from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[2]"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[4]"},{"type":"text","value":". A function filter makes\nthe plan read its whole source, so the graph holds every row and the top-K can\nalways reach the next eligible row. A mutant that sends this plan through the\nbounded prefix path (and ignores the joined filter) survives: it is equivalent\nwithin this domain, because #2055's hazard needs a bounded read that left an\neligible row out. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":"'s gate fails the witness at creation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutants on the merged code"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (ordered-lifecycle, loader, ordered-work and\npagination oracles, 724 tests):"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcome"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"full-source"},{"type":"text","value":" request settles synchronously"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assertion failure, 1 test: warm readiness, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expected 'ready' to be 'loading'"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No settled-request check"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assertion failure, 1 test: warm readiness"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Promise results settle synchronously"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assertion failures, 275 tests"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Initial full-source excluded ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assertion failures, 9 tests"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bounded prefix repair disjunct dropped (pre-#2055)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assertion failures, 2 tests (#2055's loader and NaN pagination cases)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full-source repair on a bounded-prefix plan settles synchronously"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Survival, permitted by the contract. #1896's cut \"does not apply to repair\", which scopes the promise rather than requiring asynchronous timing. The narrow gate keeps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":"'s timing by choice."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"orc-012-requirement-audit","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-012 requirement audit"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requirement"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcome"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-001"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Applicable. The law and its authority are above. The claim is limited to the initial full-source load; later full-source fallback, repair, replay, explicit window moves, and framework render timing are unchanged."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-002"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Applicable. The expected observation is the same two-valued finite reference as the #1896 cells: ready with ids [1, 2] for literal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", loading with no rows for a Promise. The ids come from a three-row source ordered by rank, not from the production comparator."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-003"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Applicable. The new section opens with the law, the model, the driver's request-shape check, and the excluded neighbouring cases. The file's opening prose states the revised cut."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-004"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Applicable. A finite matrix: 4 features × 2 settlements on an on-demand source, 4 eager cells, and 4 replay cells. Each cell is enumerated; the full-source request shape is asserted, so a plan that silently took the ordered path fails. The residual-predicate feature is not user-constructible and is outside this grammar."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-005"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Applicable. The driver calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"preload()"},{"type":"text","value":" on a real live query and observes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toArray"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" at the same call, before awaiting."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-006"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Applicable. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" behavior and three hostile mutants fail at the intended checkpoint (table above)."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-007"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not applicable. The new cells are a finite matrix, not a generated property."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-008"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not applicable. No stateful reference model changes."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-009"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Applicable. \"Initial full-source load\" means the first "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"full-source"},{"type":"text","value":" request from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start()"},{"type":"text","value":" before any source request settles. It is not a production type; the loader derives it from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasSettledSourceRequest"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"needsOrderingRepair"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-010"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Applicable. The drivers use the file's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishOracleCleanup"},{"type":"text","value":", which keeps the primary failure and every cleanup error in an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AggregateError"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-011"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not applicable. No shared-fault hypothesis was named."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-013"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not applicable. No threshold or range law."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-014"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Applicable, limited. The on-demand cells use a controlled provider. The eager cells and the React cell use real eager Collections. No adapter package (Query Collection, Electric) is exercised here."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"unresolved","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unresolved"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A full-source fallback inside the initial ordered chain, such as the warm\nreadiness case's inexpressible null boundary, stays asynchronous. #1896's\noracle pins that timing; making it synchronous would be a separate decision."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"groupBy"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"having"},{"type":"text","value":" set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requiresFullSource"},{"type":"text","value":" but were not added as cells."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No law fixes the timing of a full-source repair on an eager source. The gate\nkeeps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":"'s asynchronous timing; making it synchronous would be a separate\ndecision with its own publication evidence."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"initial-full-source-ordered-load-readiness-review","text":"Initial full-source ordered load readiness review","level":1},{"id":"contract-and-evidence","text":"Contract and evidence","level":2},{"id":"observations","text":"Observations","level":2},{"id":"mutant-results","text":"Mutant results","level":2},{"id":"after-merging-2055","text":"After merging #2055","level":2},{"id":"orc-012-requirement-audit","text":"ORC-012 requirement audit","level":2},{"id":"unresolved","text":"Unresolved","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# Initial full-source ordered load readiness review\n\nEvidence by revision, on `fix-full-source-sync-readiness`:\n\n- First campaign: oracle commit `bc2c9438b`, production fix `a73a35bac`. The\n  RED results on `main` and the first mutant results refer to this campaign.\n- After merging `main` with #2055 (merge `5d4802052`): the eager and\n  joined-filter witnesses and the merged-code mutant results in \"After merging\n  #2055\" were run on `afef46744`, which adds those witnesses to `5d4802052`.\n- After merging `main` with #2060 (merge `a0537aa0e`): the ordered-lifecycle\n  and loader oracles (332 tests) and every CI test group passed on\n  `a0537aa0e`. The production gate is unchanged from `afef46744`.\n\n## Contract and evidence\n\n#1896 made an ordered, limited live query ready in the call that creates it\nwhen every acquisition for its initial window returns literal `true` after\nits establishing receipts apply. Its stated exceptions are explicit window\nmoves, repair, truncate replay, and framework render timing.\n\nA plan that requires the full source (an inner or right join, a functional or\nresidual predicate, grouping, `having`, `distinct`, an indirect order, or a\ncustom string comparator) loads its ordered source with one filtered\nfull-source request from `OrderedSourceLoader.start()`. The loader classified\nevery `full-source` request as an authoritative repair, so this initial load\nwas excluded from the synchronous cut. On `main`, such a query over an eager\nsource, or over an on-demand source whose `loadSubset` returns `true`, reported\n`loading` with no rows at creation.\n\nThe authority for the law is the #1896 cut in\n`packages/db/src/query/live/ARCHITECTURE.md` (initial readiness section) and\nthe #1896 pull request description, which states the rule for every ordered\nand limited query whose required source work finishes synchronously. This\nchange revises that section to name the initial full-source load and a later\nfull-source fallback explicitly.\n\nThe fix classifies by purpose. The first full-source request of a loader that\nhas not settled a source request and owes no ordering repair is an initial\nload and may settle synchronously. A later full-source request keeps the\nasynchronous path.\n\n## Observations\n\n| Cell | `main` | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| On-demand, synchronous, 4 features (inner join, `fn.where`, `distinct`, custom collation) | `{\"rows\":[],\"status\":\"loading\"}` | `{\"rows\":[1,2],\"status\":\"ready\"}` |\n| On-demand, Promise, 4 features | loading | loading |\n| Eager source, 4 features | `{\"rows\":[],\"status\":\"loading\"}` | `{\"rows\":[1,2],\"status\":\"ready\"}` |\n| Truncate replay, 4 features | prior window at the replay call, replacement a task later | same |\n| Warm readiness: full-source fallback after a settled ordered request (existing case) | loading | loading |\n| React first layout commit, `fn.where` + `orderBy` + `limit` | see review head | `{ ids: ['1','2'], status: 'ready' }` |\n\n## Mutant results\n\nEach mutant ran against `tests/query/ordered-lifecycle-oracle.property.test.ts`.\n\n| Mutant | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| Gate keyed on request kind: every `full-source` request settles synchronously | Assertion failure: warm readiness case, `expected 'ready' to be 'loading'` |\n| Promise results may settle synchronously | Assertion failures in 145 tests |\n| Initial full-source load still excluded (the `main` behavior) | Assertion failures in the 4 synchronous on-demand cells |\n| Initial-load test without the settled-request condition | Assertion failure: warm readiness case |\n\nThe truncate replay cells do not distinguish the kind-based mutant: replay\npublishes through the subscription's replay barrier, not this loader gate. The\nwarm readiness case is the distinguishing neighbour for that design.\n\n## After merging #2055\n\n**Main check.** Before the merge, this branch's witnesses ran on `main` at\n`25201da6c` (which includes #2027 and #2055). All 8 synchronous full-source\ncells and the React first-commit witness still failed, for example\n`Expected {\"rows\":[1,2],\"status\":\"ready\"}, received {\"rows\":[],\"status\":\"loading\"}`\nand `expected { ids: [], status: 'loading' } to deeply equal { ids: [ '1', '2' ],\nstatus: 'ready' }`. #2027 changed the infinite-query hooks' `startSync`, not this\ngate, so the gap remained.\n\n**Combined gate.** An initial load of any kind, and an eager bounded\nordered-prefix repair (#2055), settle synchronously on literal `true`:\n\n```ts\n(!isAuthoritativeRepair ||\n  isInitialFullSource ||\n  (this.readsBoundedPrefix && !isFullSource))\n```\n\n**Changed expectation.** #2055 added `keeps an eager full-source ordered window\nloading until its load settles`, pinning `main`'s asynchronous timing while its\nown scope stayed narrow. Recorded predictions before the edit: `main` and #2055\npredict `{loading, 0 rows}` at creation; this branch's law predicts\n`{ready, [4, 3]}`. The authority is #1896's rule and the user's decision to close\nthis gap. The test is now `publishes an eager full-source ordered window at\ncreation`.\n\n**Joined-filter interaction.** `keeps the first eligible joined rows after a\nsynchronous full-source load` combines a function filter with #2055's\nLEFT-joined filter history: a label-only update to distant row 10, then a delete\nof visible row 2. The window moves from `[2]` to `[4]`. A function filter makes\nthe plan read its whole source, so the graph holds every row and the top-K can\nalways reach the next eligible row. A mutant that sends this plan through the\nbounded prefix path (and ignores the joined filter) survives: it is equivalent\nwithin this domain, because #2055's hazard needs a bounded read that left an\neligible row out. `main`'s gate fails the witness at creation.\n\n**Mutants on the merged code** (ordered-lifecycle, loader, ordered-work and\npagination oracles, 724 tests):\n\n| Mutant | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| Every `full-source` request settles synchronously | Assertion failure, 1 test: warm readiness, `expected 'ready' to be 'loading'` |\n| No settled-request check | Assertion failure, 1 test: warm readiness |\n| Promise results settle synchronously | Assertion failures, 275 tests |\n| Initial full-source excluded (`main`) | Assertion failures, 9 tests |\n| Bounded prefix repair disjunct dropped (pre-#2055) | Assertion failures, 2 tests (#2055's loader and NaN pagination cases) |\n| Full-source repair on a bounded-prefix plan settles synchronously | Survival, permitted by the contract. #1896's cut \"does not apply to repair\", which scopes the promise rather than requiring asynchronous timing. The narrow gate keeps `main`'s timing by choice. |\n\n## ORC-012 requirement audit\n\n| Requirement | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| ORC-001 | Applicable. The law and its authority are above. The claim is limited to the initial full-source load; later full-source fallback, repair, replay, explicit window moves, and framework render timing are unchanged. |\n| ORC-002 | Applicable. The expected observation is the same two-valued finite reference as the #1896 cells: ready with ids [1, 2] for literal `true`, loading with no rows for a Promise. The ids come from a three-row source ordered by rank, not from the production comparator. |\n| ORC-003 | Applicable. The new section opens with the law, the model, the driver's request-shape check, and the excluded neighbouring cases. The file's opening prose states the revised cut. |\n| ORC-004 | Applicable. A finite matrix: 4 features × 2 settlements on an on-demand source, 4 eager cells, and 4 replay cells. Each cell is enumerated; the full-source request shape is asserted, so a plan that silently took the ordered path fails. The residual-predicate feature is not user-constructible and is outside this grammar. |\n| ORC-005 | Applicable. The driver calls `preload()` on a real live query and observes `toArray` and `status` at the same call, before awaiting. |\n| ORC-006 | Applicable. The `main` behavior and three hostile mutants fail at the intended checkpoint (table above). |\n| ORC-007 | Not applicable. The new cells are a finite matrix, not a generated property. |\n| ORC-008 | Not applicable. No stateful reference model changes. |\n| ORC-009 | Applicable. \"Initial full-source load\" means the first `full-source` request from `start()` before any source request settles. It is not a production type; the loader derives it from `hasSettledSourceRequest` and `needsOrderingRepair`. |\n| ORC-010 | Applicable. The drivers use the file's `finishOracleCleanup`, which keeps the primary failure and every cleanup error in an `AggregateError`. |\n| ORC-011 | Not applicable. No shared-fault hypothesis was named. |\n| ORC-013 | Not applicable. No threshold or range law. |\n| ORC-014 | Applicable, limited. The on-demand cells use a controlled provider. The eager cells and the React cell use real eager Collections. No adapter package (Query Collection, Electric) is exercised here. |\n\n## Unresolved\n\n- A full-source fallback inside the initial ordered chain, such as the warm\n  readiness case's inexpressible null boundary, stays asynchronous. #1896's\n  oracle pins that timing; making it synchronous would be a separate decision.\n- `groupBy` and `having` set `requiresFullSource` but were not added as cells.\n- No law fixes the timing of a full-source repair on an eager source. The gate\n  keeps `main`'s asynchronous timing; making it synchronous would be a separate\n  decision with its own publication evidence.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# Initial full-source ordered load readiness review\n\nEvidence by revision, on `fix-full-source-sync-readiness`:\n\n- First campaign: oracle commit `bc2c9438b`, production fix `a73a35bac`. The\n  RED results on `main` and the first mutant results refer to this campaign.\n- After merging `main` with #2055 (merge `5d4802052`): the eager and\n  joined-filter witnesses and the merged-code mutant results in \"After merging\n  #2055\" were run on `afef46744`, which adds those witnesses to `5d4802052`.\n- After merging `main` with #2060 (merge `a0537aa0e`): the ordered-lifecycle\n  and loader oracles (332 tests) and every CI test group passed on\n  `a0537aa0e`. The production gate is unchanged from `afef46744`.\n\n## Contract and evidence\n\n#1896 made an ordered, limited live query ready in the call that creates it\nwhen every acquisition for its initial window returns literal `true` after\nits establishing receipts apply. Its stated exceptions are explicit window\nmoves, repair, truncate replay, and framework render timing.\n\nA plan that requires the full source (an inner or right join, a functional or\nresidual predicate, grouping, `having`, `distinct`, an indirect order, or a\ncustom string comparator) loads its ordered source with one filtered\nfull-source request from `OrderedSourceLoader.start()`. The loader classified\nevery `full-source` request as an authoritative repair, so this initial load\nwas excluded from the synchronous cut. On `main`, such a query over an eager\nsource, or over an on-demand source whose `loadSubset` returns `true`, reported\n`loading` with no rows at creation.\n\nThe authority for the law is the #1896 cut in\n`packages/db/src/query/live/ARCHITECTURE.md` (initial readiness section) and\nthe #1896 pull request description, which states the rule for every ordered\nand limited query whose required source work finishes synchronously. This\nchange revises that section to name the initial full-source load and a later\nfull-source fallback explicitly.\n\nThe fix classifies by purpose. The first full-source request of a loader that\nhas not settled a source request and owes no ordering repair is an initial\nload and may settle synchronously. A later full-source request keeps the\nasynchronous path.\n\n## Observations\n\n| Cell | `main` | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| On-demand, synchronous, 4 features (inner join, `fn.where`, `distinct`, custom collation) | `{\"rows\":[],\"status\":\"loading\"}` | `{\"rows\":[1,2],\"status\":\"ready\"}` |\n| On-demand, Promise, 4 features | loading | loading |\n| Eager source, 4 features | `{\"rows\":[],\"status\":\"loading\"}` | `{\"rows\":[1,2],\"status\":\"ready\"}` |\n| Truncate replay, 4 features | prior window at the replay call, replacement a task later | same |\n| Warm readiness: full-source fallback after a settled ordered request (existing case) | loading | loading |\n| React first layout commit, `fn.where` + `orderBy` + `limit` | see review head | `{ ids: ['1','2'], status: 'ready' }` |\n\n## Mutant results\n\nEach mutant ran against `tests/query/ordered-lifecycle-oracle.property.test.ts`.\n\n| Mutant | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| Gate keyed on request kind: every `full-source` request settles synchronously | Assertion failure: warm readiness case, `expected 'ready' to be 'loading'` |\n| Promise results may settle synchronously | Assertion failures in 145 tests |\n| Initial full-source load still excluded (the `main` behavior) | Assertion failures in the 4 synchronous on-demand cells |\n| Initial-load test without the settled-request condition | Assertion failure: warm readiness case |\n\nThe truncate replay cells do not distinguish the kind-based mutant: replay\npublishes through the subscription's replay barrier, not this loader gate. The\nwarm readiness case is the distinguishing neighbour for that design.\n\n## After merging #2055\n\n**Main check.** Before the merge, this branch's witnesses ran on `main` at\n`25201da6c` (which includes #2027 and #2055). All 8 synchronous full-source\ncells and the React first-commit witness still failed, for example\n`Expected {\"rows\":[1,2],\"status\":\"ready\"}, received {\"rows\":[],\"status\":\"loading\"}`\nand `expected { ids: [], status: 'loading' } to deeply equal { ids: [ '1', '2' ],\nstatus: 'ready' }`. #2027 changed the infinite-query hooks' `startSync`, not this\ngate, so the gap remained.\n\n**Combined gate.** An initial load of any kind, and an eager bounded\nordered-prefix repair (#2055), settle synchronously on literal `true`:\n\n```ts\n(!isAuthoritativeRepair ||\n  isInitialFullSource ||\n  (this.readsBoundedPrefix && !isFullSource))\n```\n\n**Changed expectation.** #2055 added `keeps an eager full-source ordered window\nloading until its load settles`, pinning `main`'s asynchronous timing while its\nown scope stayed narrow. Recorded predictions before the edit: `main` and #2055\npredict `{loading, 0 rows}` at creation; this branch's law predicts\n`{ready, [4, 3]}`. The authority is #1896's rule and the user's decision to close\nthis gap. The test is now `publishes an eager full-source ordered window at\ncreation`.\n\n**Joined-filter interaction.** `keeps the first eligible joined rows after a\nsynchronous full-source load` combines a function filter with #2055's\nLEFT-joined filter history: a label-only update to distant row 10, then a delete\nof visible row 2. The window moves from `[2]` to `[4]`. A function filter makes\nthe plan read its whole source, so the graph holds every row and the top-K can\nalways reach the next eligible row. A mutant that sends this plan through the\nbounded prefix path (and ignores the joined filter) survives: it is equivalent\nwithin this domain, because #2055's hazard needs a bounded read that left an\neligible row out. `main`'s gate fails the witness at creation.\n\n**Mutants on the merged code** (ordered-lifecycle, loader, ordered-work and\npagination oracles, 724 tests):\n\n| Mutant | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| Every `full-source` request settles synchronously | Assertion failure, 1 test: warm readiness, `expected 'ready' to be 'loading'` |\n| No settled-request check | Assertion failure, 1 test: warm readiness |\n| Promise results settle synchronously | Assertion failures, 275 tests |\n| Initial full-source excluded (`main`) | Assertion failures, 9 tests |\n| Bounded prefix repair disjunct dropped (pre-#2055) | Assertion failures, 2 tests (#2055's loader and NaN pagination cases) |\n| Full-source repair on a bounded-prefix plan settles synchronously | Survival, permitted by the contract. #1896's cut \"does not apply to repair\", which scopes the promise rather than requiring asynchronous timing. The narrow gate keeps `main`'s timing by choice. |\n\n## ORC-012 requirement audit\n\n| Requirement | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| ORC-001 | Applicable. The law and its authority are above. The claim is limited to the initial full-source load; later full-source fallback, repair, replay, explicit window moves, and framework render timing are unchanged. |\n| ORC-002 | Applicable. The expected observation is the same two-valued finite reference as the #1896 cells: ready with ids [1, 2] for literal `true`, loading with no rows for a Promise. The ids come from a three-row source ordered by rank, not from the production comparator. |\n| ORC-003 | Applicable. The new section opens with the law, the model, the driver's request-shape check, and the excluded neighbouring cases. The file's opening prose states the revised cut. |\n| ORC-004 | Applicable. A finite matrix: 4 features × 2 settlements on an on-demand source, 4 eager cells, and 4 replay cells. Each cell is enumerated; the full-source request shape is asserted, so a plan that silently took the ordered path fails. The residual-predicate feature is not user-constructible and is outside this grammar. |\n| ORC-005 | Applicable. The driver calls `preload()` on a real live query and observes `toArray` and `status` at the same call, before awaiting. |\n| ORC-006 | Applicable. The `main` behavior and three hostile mutants fail at the intended checkpoint (table above). |\n| ORC-007 | Not applicable. The new cells are a finite matrix, not a generated property. |\n| ORC-008 | Not applicable. No stateful reference model changes. |\n| ORC-009 | Applicable. \"Initial full-source load\" means the first `full-source` request from `start()` before any source request settles. It is not a production type; the loader derives it from `hasSettledSourceRequest` and `needsOrderingRepair`. |\n| ORC-010 | Applicable. The drivers use the file's `finishOracleCleanup`, which keeps the primary failure and every cleanup error in an `AggregateError`. |\n| ORC-011 | Not applicable. No shared-fault hypothesis was named. |\n| ORC-013 | Not applicable. No threshold or range law. |\n| ORC-014 | Applicable, limited. The on-demand cells use a controlled provider. The eager cells and the React cell use real eager Collections. No adapter package (Query Collection, Electric) is exercised here. |\n\n## Unresolved\n\n- A full-source fallback inside the initial ordered chain, such as the warm\n  readiness case's inexpressible null boundary, stays asynchronous. #1896's\n  oracle pins that timing; making it synchronous would be a separate decision.\n- `groupBy` and `having` set `requiresFullSource` but were not added as cells.\n- No law fixes the timing of a full-source repair on an eager source. The gate\n  keeps `main`'s asynchronous timing; making it synchronous would be a separate\n  decision with its own publication evidence.\n"}
